# Story: of six open windows a person wants three beside each other. ⌃⌥G, a few letters, ⌘↩, three times; ↩. They stand side by side in
# the order ticked and fill the screen. What was docked stays docked. One of the three was in the Dock. One undo takes it all back.
# Reference: IDEAS I18; QUESTIONS Q29, 9; board 0.12. Window ids start at 101.
# The command by itself, with nothing else touched, is collab/scenarios/wanted/I18-a-few-windows-in-one-step.sim, which waits for board 0.5.
open Safari
open Notes
open Mail
open Music
open Preview
open Xcode
dock 106 left
dock 102 right
minimize 104
focus 105
# The line under the rows says how, before anybody asks.
find
expect ok
expect replied ticks a window: two to four are docked side by side
finder-type mai
finder-tick
expect ok
# A tick clears the field and the whole list shows again.
expect replied go to:
expect replied [1]
finder-type saf
finder-tick
expect replied docks these 2 side by side
finder-type mus
finder-tick
expect replied docks these 3 side by side
# Nothing has moved so far.
expect floating 103
expect floating 101
finder-choose
expect ok
expect moved-once
expect count docked 5
expect left-of 103 101
expect left-of 101 104
expect visible 104
expect focused 103
# What was docked is still docked, out of view for now.
expect docked 106
expect docked 102
expect hidden 106
# Everything: the group stands at the right end.
show-all
expect left-of 102 103
back
expect left-of 103 101
expect hidden 102
# One step back for all of it: the windows, the view, the keyboard.
undo
expect ok
expect count docked 2
expect floating 103
expect visible 106
expect focused 105
# A fifth is refused in words, and so is what is no window.
find
finder-tick 1
finder-tick 2
finder-tick 3
finder-tick 4
finder-tick 5
expect fail
expect replied Four at the most
finder-cancel
# With one ticked, Return goes there as if it had been chosen.
find
finder-type note
finder-tick
finder-type prev
finder-choose
expect focused 102
expect count docked 2
